{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHWAD59UKWnxFgLhcaaWXp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R10 — Backend review — Phase 1 identity substrate\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** Review for Phase 1\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T06, T07, T08, T09\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n8\t**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n9\t\n10\t## Purpose\n11\t\n12\tThis review certifies that Phase 1 delivers a unified identity substrate that all later phases can build on without re-litigating: stable id types for every entity kind, a resolver that returns ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary picks, identity payloads serialized in MCP responses with legacy compatibility, and a full correctness + P99 budget test matrix. It is the gate Phase 2 (event log) depends on because events that reference unstable names cannot be replayed.\n13\t\n14\t## Inputs to read\n15\t\n16\t- Every artifact produced by T06, T07, T08, T09:\n17\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs`\n18\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`\n19\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs`\n20\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs`\n21\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs`\n22\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs`\n23\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs`\n24\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`\n25\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs`\n26\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs`\n27\t- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy: `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model`; cross-checks against `## Design Thesis`, `## System Architecture`, and `## MCP Surface`.\n28\t- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (hard limits, error handling, naming, no broken windows, tests as documentation) and `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md` items relevant to backend phases.\n29\t- T02 compatibility policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`) — verify the per-tool classification was updated for any tool that gained identity payloads in T08.\n30\t- T04 baseline metrics (`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json`) — verify budget tests reference these numbers.\n31\t\n32\t## Review procedure\n33\t\n34\t1. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and confirm the full workspace compiles without new warnings.\n35\t2. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver_tests`; record pass/fail per named test.\n36\t3. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::budget_tests -- --include-ignored` and record the measured P99 per budget test alongside the 2ms target and the baseline number from T04.\n37\t4. Run `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization rpc::identity_payload` to confirm the MCP wiring tests pass.\n38\t5. Open `kinds.rs` and verify all seven identity kinds exist (File, Symbol, Doc, Section, Event, Memory, ContextHandle) by literal grep for each struct name.\n39\t6. Open `ambiguity.rs` and verify `ResolveOutcome` has the three variants (`Unique`, `Ambiguous`, `NotFound`) and that `AmbiguityReport` carries a `disambiguation_hint`.\n40\t7. Open `serialization.rs` and `identity_payload.rs` and confirm legacy name fields are preserved alongside new identity payloads on at least one workflow tool response (per T02 compatibility policy).\n41\t8. Open `resolver_tests.rs` and confirm the ten spec-mandated test cases (renames, moves, duplicates, branch changes, legacy compat, event-ref round-trip) are present by name.\n42\t9. Run `wc -l` on every Phase 1 source file and confirm each is ≤800 lines.\n43\t10. Grep all Phase 1 files for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, and unjustified `#[allow(...)]` attributes. Flag every hit.\n44\t11. Inspect resolver error types and confirm no bare `String` errors leak through the public API (every error is a typed `ResolveError` variant).\n45\t12. Cross-check that doc citations in module-level docs reference the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading.\n46\t\n47\t## Required sections in the review output file\n48\t\n49\tThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n50\t\n51\t- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix for Phase 1 deliverables (stable ids per kind, resolver, ambiguity diagnostics, MCP serialization, legacy compatibility shim, four test categories). One row per deliverable with evidence column citing the artifact and the literal test name or struct name.\n52\t- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits: `wc -l` per file, forbidden token grep, suppression audit, naming audit on public API surface.\n53\t- `## P99 budget evidence` — measured P99 numbers from `cargo test -- --include-ignored` for every budget test, alongside the 2ms target and the relevant baseline number from `baseline_metrics.json`. Verdict per metric: `within budget` or `over budget`.\n54\t- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks opened in this build (never deferred outside).\n55\t- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n56\t\n57\t## Verification\n58\t\n59\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where Phase 2 tasks can read it.\n60\t- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms spec alignment is a dedicated section, not buried in prose.\n61\t- `grep -q '## Coding-standard alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the standards audit was performed under a dedicated heading.\n62\t- `grep -q '## P99 budget evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the 2ms hot-path budget from spec §Phase 1 DoD was measured and recorded.\n63\t- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the review concludes with a binding verdict.\n64\t\n65\t## Definition of done\n66\t\n67\t- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n68\t- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n69\t- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"beca6473-0a8b-4b3f-8c29-18a74c665d8f","uuid":"8cdbbd66-62c6-412d-b4b7-ed0464839a5b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T04:18:47.947Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R10.md","content":"# R10 — Backend review — Phase 1 identity substrate\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase 1\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T06, T07, T08, T09\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review certifies that Phase 1 delivers a unified identity substrate that all later phases can build on without re-litigating: stable id types for every entity kind, a resolver that returns ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary picks, identity payloads serialized in MCP responses with legacy compatibility, and a full correctness + P99 budget test matrix. It is the gate Phase 2 (event log) depends on because events that reference unstable names cannot be replayed.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by T06, T07, T08, T09:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs`\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy: `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model`; cross-checks against `## Design Thesis`, `## System Architecture`, and `## MCP Surface`.\n- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (hard limits, error handling, naming, no broken windows, tests as documentation) and `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md` items relevant to backend phases.\n- T02 compatibility policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`) — verify the per-tool classification was updated for any tool that gained identity payloads in T08.\n- T04 baseline metrics (`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json`) — verify budget tests reference these numbers.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and confirm the full workspace compiles without new warnings.\n2. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver_tests`; record pass/fail per named test.\n3. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::budget_tests -- --include-ignored` and record the measured P99 per budget test alongside the 2ms target and the baseline number from T04.\n4. Run `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization rpc::identity_payload` to confirm the MCP wiring tests pass.\n5. Open `kinds.rs` and verify all seven identity kinds exist (File, Symbol, Doc, Section, Event, Memory, ContextHandle) by literal grep for each struct name.\n6. Open `ambiguity.rs` and verify `ResolveOutcome` has the three variants (`Unique`, `Ambiguous`, `NotFound`) and that `AmbiguityReport` carries a `disambiguation_hint`.\n7. Open `serialization.rs` and `identity_payload.rs` and confirm legacy name fields are preserved alongside new identity payloads on at least one workflow tool response (per T02 compatibility policy).\n8. Open `resolver_tests.rs` and confirm the ten spec-mandated test cases (renames, moves, duplicates, branch changes, legacy compat, event-ref round-trip) are present by name.\n9. Run `wc -l` on every Phase 1 source file and confirm each is ≤800 lines.\n10. Grep all Phase 1 files for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, and unjustified `#[allow(...)]` attributes. Flag every hit.\n11. Inspect resolver error types and confirm no bare `String` errors leak through the public API (every error is a typed `ResolveError` variant).\n12. Cross-check that doc citations in module-level docs reference the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix for Phase 1 deliverables (stable ids per kind, resolver, ambiguity diagnostics, MCP serialization, legacy compatibility shim, four test categories). One row per deliverable with evidence column citing the artifact and the literal test name or struct name.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits: `wc -l` per file, forbidden token grep, suppression audit, naming audit on public API surface.\n- `## P99 budget evidence` — measured P99 numbers from `cargo test -- --include-ignored` for every budget test, alongside the 2ms target and the relevant baseline number from `baseline_metrics.json`. Verdict per metric: `within budget` or `over budget`.\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks opened in this build (never deferred outside).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where Phase 2 tasks can read it.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms spec alignment is a dedicated section, not buried in prose.\n- `grep -q '## Coding-standard alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the standards audit was performed under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## P99 budget evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the 2ms hot-path budget from spec §Phase 1 DoD was measured and recorded.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R10-identity.md` — confirms the review concludes with a binding verdict.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
